  "$comment": "How each calibre family sounds, as layers the synth plays now and a sample replaces later (ids of checklist-sons.md 5.1). close = crack (supersonic N-wave or the muzzle snap, highpass), blast (the mid 'slap', lowpass) and body (the low thump, a sine sweep). far = what is left at 50 m and more: a lowpassed boom and its echoes. tail_in / tail_out = the room or the open field answering. Seconds are the exponential fall to -60 dB. Values chosen by the SDK from the real character of each calibre (see the checklist's 'Como deve soar'); referenceJ is the muzzle energy the numbers are written for.",
